8:3: tamber-motion-axis: a duration or an easing is written into its `transition` or `animation` at build, so it has one value: no `when` (vary the row instead)
10:3: tamber-motion-axis: a duration or an easing is written into its `transition` or `animation` at build, so it has one value: no `when` (vary the row instead)
12:27: tamber-kind: `cubic-bezier(2, 0, 0, 1)` is no easing a transition takes
13:24: tamber-kind: `steps(0)` is no easing a transition takes
14:29: tamber-kind: a duration is a time, `150ms` or `0.15s`
15:31: tamber-kind: `ink` is not a duration
16:27: tamber-kind: `12px`: a duration is in `ms` or `s`
17:28: tamber-unknown-token: `bounce` is no easing token or keyword
18:25: tamber-kind: `steps(2, bogus)` is no easing a transition takes
19:24: tamber-kind: `-exact-spring(-1, 26, 1)` is no easing a transition takes
20:26: tamber-kind: `linear()` is no easing a transition takes
21:3: tamber-motion-name: `fast`: a duration's or an easing's name is dotted (`duration.fast`), so a `transition` or `animation` reads it as the token wherever it stands, never as a property, a keyframes name or a keyword
23:3: tamber-motion-name: `standard`: a duration's or an easing's name is dotted (`easing.standard`), so a `transition` or `animation` reads it as the token wherever it stands, never as a property, a keyframes name or a keyword
